  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own multi-year '5 (Five) Years Key Financial Data & Ratios- JBPLC. (Solo)' summary table (audited), Solo basis. Consolidated basis also published in the same report ('FIVE YEARS PERFORMANCE (CONSOLIDATED)', p.109-111) with slightly larger figures (e.g. FY2024 total assets BDT 366,487.71mn Consolidated vs BDT 366,021.48mn Solo here) -- Solo used for consistency with 2011-2023. Tax expense is taken from the report's separate 'Financial Highlights' table (p.108), which reports it explicitly, and cross-validated as Profit before tax (5,848.35) minus Profit after tax (2,794.00) = 3,054.35 exactly. tier1_ratio_pct's cell in this report's own table is corrupted by a text-extraction artifact ('217' instead of '12.17'); the value 12.17 used here is reconstructed from the FY2025 annual report's FY2024 comparative column, and is internally consistent with this report's own Tier-1 capital (23,307.35) / RWA (191,521.42) = 12.17%. EPS of 3.17 is this bank's own contemporaneously-reported figure for FY2024; the FY2025 annual report later restates FY2024 EPS down to 2.97 following BAS 33's retrospective-restatement requirement after the 6.50% FY2024 bonus share issue (paid out in 2025, raising paid-up capital from 8,820.07mn to 9,393.38mn) -- the restated figure is not used here per this project's contemporaneous-figures rule (see sources.json for the full restatement chain, which also affects FY2023's stored EPS when viewed from this later report). Book value/NAV per share is NOT retroactively restated for bonus issues in this bank's tables (24.70 for FY2024 is consistent across every report that shows it).",
